","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"3e2bfa636afe16abf33bb8c5fc2675a84e1f6df3f655063715c678c6d6e332c1"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T1","usage":{"input_tokens":14080,"output_tokens":1139,"requests":2}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"54403012275ac1410132111719f1bd8bf3896a048dad50d07dbdaea7fe51f4c7"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":13399,"output_tokens":570,"requests":2}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"01f5788a9b3056a3ffd8291541c92500774dcf1dc776f2e827b88648fcca8eb2"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G6","usage":{"input_tokens":78734,"output_tokens":2963,"requests":6}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"ea4c9e9902b7c6cf8e1c9af80d983b1e5b75362218c4cbfdc3744aa2fccdf176"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T5c","usage":{"input_tokens":24211,"output_tokens":1023,"requests":3}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"01e94e1fd88a77bd90e908656e7d9cdd5c3c928d6639630431c1400d5a3672b7"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T3","usage":{"input_tokens":35320,"output_tokens":1322,"requests":4}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"37f7ce12a3da1b61d0f9cada223fb67539af70cadbdc409079021c36610cf2fe"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T10","usage":{"input_tokens":298956,"output_tokens":4249,"requests":6}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate ALL THREE layers that define REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY for the mcp service — the SSM-sourced .env (env_file / --env-file, emitted by fetch-secrets.sh), the compose `environment:` override, and the autodeploy `docker run -e` override — and state which one is retained as the single owner so the fix cannot accidentally leave .env's review-bot value as the survivor.","cohort":["T10"],"criteria":["T10"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0111,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Both a compose-level environment entry and the blue-green docker run invocation in infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh supply the variable.'","fetch-secrets.sh:271 unconditionally emits `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY=${signing_key_path}` (the rebar-bot-signing-key path) into the SSM-sourced .env consumed by every service.","docker-compose.yml mcp service: `env_file: - .env` (line 388) PLUS explicit `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY: \"/run/secrets/opcert-ed25519-key\"` (line 434) — the explicit entry is the last-wins override of the .env value.","autodeploy.sh mcp_run_new: `--env-file \"$COMPOSE_DIR/.env\"` (line 498) PLUS `-e REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY=/run/secrets/opcert-ed25519-key` (line 513) — same override shape.","The two layers the plan names both set the CORRECT value; the .env (env_file) is the source of the review-bot value the plan describes as the conflicting definition."],"finding":"The plan's root-cause enumeration ('Where it comes from') names only two contributing layers (the compose `environment:` entry and the autodeploy `docker run -e`), but BOTH of those already carry the CORRECT value (/run/secrets/opcert-ed25519-key). The CONFLICTING review-bot value is supplied by a third, unnamed layer: the SSM-sourced .env delivered via `env_file:` (compose) and `--env-file` (autodeploy), which fetch-secrets.sh emits unconditionally for every .env consumer. A fix that de-duplicates without accounting for the .env layer risks removing the wrong definition and flipping the effective value.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcbf9c4d51439d55d","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Where it comes from' / AC1 ('defines REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY exactly ONCE, from a single owning layer')","norm_id":"n1aef44844ba9ca49","priority":0.8889,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor reads 'have exactly one owner' + the two named layers, deletes the compose/autodeploy explicit override as the apparent duplicate, and the mcp service then inherits the review-bot key path from .env — flipping the effective value to a path that does not exist in-container and aborting mcp startup (the exact fail-closed outage the plan warns about)."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In 'Where it comes from', add the .env/env_file layer (fetch-secrets.sh:271) as the source of the conflicting review-bot value, and make AC1 explicit that the retained owner must resolve to /run/secrets/opcert-ed25519-key (e.g. keep the per-service override and/or stop emitting the bot value into .env for the mcp consumer), not merely 'delete a duplicate'.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify where the uniqueness check runs and when it fires (deploy-time gate in autodeploy.sh, CI step, or container-startup assertion) so it cannot silently be skipped on future edits.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.28,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'A check fails if the variable is ever defined more than once for this service, so the condition cannot silently return.'","The plan names no execution point (deploy pipeline, autodeploy.sh, container startup) for this check."],"finding":"AC4 introduces a new guard ('A check fails if the variable is ever defined more than once for this service') but does not specify who owns that check or when it fires — deploy-time gate, CI step, or a runtime startup assertion. Without a defined owner and trigger, the guard is itself shared-state whose lifecycle is undefined and it could silently never run.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd142c037cebcfcac","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, line 4 ('A check fails if the variable is ever defined more than once for this service')","norm_id":"nfc9f9917e0581e26","priority":0.67,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["If the uniqueness check lives only in a manual test run and not in the deploy path, a future edit to compose or autodeploy.sh re-introduces the duplicate and the guard never fires — exactly the silent-return the AC set out to prevent."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State which layer should own REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY (compose env vs. autodeploy.sh docker run), or state the decision rule the executor should apply after establishing which layers contribute.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T12","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.264,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Both a compose-level environment entry and the blue-green docker run invocation in infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh supply the variable.'","'the fix is to have exactly one owner, not to delete whichever line looks redundant' — names the property but not the owner","AC1: 'defines ... exactly ONCE, from a single owning layer' — 'single owning layer' unspecified"],"finding":"The plan decides there must be 'exactly one owning layer' but does not state WHICH layer (compose env vs. the autodeploy.sh docker run) should own REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY, deferring that design choice to the executor.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f88423c4de9390743","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"'Where it comes from' section + AC1 ('from a single owning layer')","norm_id":"nd1f321fc190745bb","priority":0.536,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor must choose between compose and autodeploy.sh as the owner and could pick the layer that does not resolve to the opcert path, or split ownership inconsistently across blue/green"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Name the intended owning layer explicitly (e.g. 'the autodeploy.sh docker run owns the opcert value; remove the compose-level entry') once the investigation confirms which la